# Per-machine configuration for the ForClim -> SorSim pipeline.
#
#   cp local.env.example local.env      # then edit local.env
#
# local.env is git-ignored: it is the one file that differs between your laptop
# and Euler, so neither `git pull` nor a branch merge can ever conflict on it.
# Both the shell wrappers (run_conversion.sh / run_analysis.sh) and the Python
# entry points read it, so an interactive `python convert_data.py ...` and an
# sbatch submission resolve identical paths.
#
# Path templates accept {case_study}, {scenario} and {cohort}.
# Anything left unset falls back to the repository-relative defaults below,
# which is what you want on a laptop.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- laptop ----
# MAINWOOD_INPUT_TEMPLATE='../data/{case_study}/inputs/{scenario}/'
# MAINWOOD_INTERMEDIATE_TEMPLATE='../data/{case_study}/intermediate/{scenario}/'
# MAINWOOD_OUTPUT_TEMPLATE='../data/{case_study}/'
# MAINWOOD_DATA_ROOT='../data'

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Euler ----
# Uncomment this block on the cluster. Check the cohort sub-folder name first:
#   ls /cluster/work/climate/amauri/Entlebuch/Results/mgmt_BAU/
# If the alive cohort is not in a folder called `alive.trees`, replace {cohort}
# with the literal folder name rather than renaming anything on disk.
#
# MAINWOOD_INPUT_TEMPLATE='/cluster/work/climate/amauri/{case_study}/Results/mgmt_{scenario}/{cohort}.trees/'
# MAINWOOD_INTERMEDIATE_TEMPLATE='/cluster/scratch/giacomov/mainwood/{case_study}/intermediate/{scenario}/'
# MAINWOOD_OUTPUT_TEMPLATE='/cluster/scratch/giacomov/mainwood/{case_study}/'
# MAINWOOD_DATA_ROOT='/cluster/scratch/giacomov/mainwood/'

# --------------------------------------------------- stand.details.csv ----
# The files in data/<region>/stand.details.csv are COPIES of a ForClim delivery
# folder (manag4giacomo). A copy goes stale silently: the committed Vaud one
# predated the area_ha column entirely, which would have made every Vaud volume
# wrong. Point this at the delivery folder and stop copying:
#
# MAINWOOD_STAND_DETAILS='/cluster/work/climate/amauri/manag4giacomo/{case_study}/stand.details.csv'
#
# Check the real layout first -- the region may be a folder, a filename prefix, or
# the file may not be per-region at all:
#   ls /cluster/work/climate/amauri/manag4giacomo/
# preflight.py prints the stand count and the area_ha total, which is the number
# every volume is scaled by: check it against what the ForClim side says they sent.

# ------------------------------------ a run against a different input folder ----
# Do NOT fork the converter to change a path. The environment beats this file, so
# one run can read from somewhere else while everything else stays as configured:
#
#   MAINWOOD_INPUT_TEMPLATE='/cluster/scratch/giacomov/mainwood/{case_study}/inputs/WOOD/{cohort}.trees/' #     ./run_conversion.sh WOOD Surselva
#
# That is how to submit several stage 1 jobs at once against different locations --
# it replaces the convert_data_plantations.py fork, which was a copy of the whole
# converter differing only in those two path lines.

# ------------------------------------------------------------ sample size ----
# How many files use_sample=True processes. Was a literal 50 in the source.
# MAINWOOD_SAMPLE_SIZE=50

# ------------------------------------------------------- sbatch defaults ----
# Used by run_conversion.sh / run_analysis.sh. Override per run on the command
# line instead of editing them: N_CORES=8 ./run_conversion.sh WOOD Entlebuch
# CONVERT_CORES=4
# CONVERT_MEM_PER_CPU=3000
# CONVERT_WALLTIME=8:00:00
# ANALYSIS_CORES=1
# ANALYSIS_MEM_PER_CPU=20000
# ANALYSIS_WALLTIME=8:00:00
# MAIL_TYPE=BEGIN,END,FAIL
